entries.description:
Let h m be the height of the flagpole. Then (h + 2) m is the length of the rope. Therefore,
\sin\theta=\frac{h}{h+2}
(h+2)\sin\theta=h
h\sin\theta+2\sin\theta=h
h-h\sin\theta=2\sin\theta
h(1-\sin\theta)=2\sin\theta
h=\frac{2\sin\theta}{1-\sin\theta}
=\frac{2\sin64^\circ}{1-\sin64^\circ}
\approx17.76\text{ m}
The flagpole is 17.76 metres tall.
